.TH CAMVIEW 1 "2026-11-22" "camview 0.2.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
camview \- lightweight RTSP camera viewer and recorder
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B camview
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B CamView
is a native Linux desktop application for viewing and recording RTSP and
RTSPS cameras. It is designed for low-power x86 machines and keeps a single
RTSP session per camera while allowing simultaneous viewing and recording.
.PP
The application uses libmpv for hardware-accelerated decoding and OpenGL for
compositing. Camera credentials are stored in
.I ~/.config/camview/config.toml
with mode 0600 and are never written to logs or shown in the user interface.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Print a short command-line help message and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-import\-m3u
Read a legacy M3U playlist from
.I ~/cameras.m3u
or
.I ~/camaras.m3u
and save the cameras to the CamView configuration. The source playlist and
user services are only read; they are never modified.
.TP
.B \-\-selftest
Create the local TLS tunnels, probe the configured cameras, decode each
substream, take a short test recording and verify it with ffprobe. This
requires the configured cameras to be reachable and is intended for
troubleshooting on the local machine.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/camview/config.toml
Camera list, recording folder and preferences. Written atomically with mode
0600.
.TP
.I ~/Videos/CamView/
Recordings, organised as
.IR camera/date/clip.mkv .
The oldest finished clips are removed when the configured global storage limit
is reached.
.TP
.I ~/Pictures/CamView/
JPEG snapshots.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/camview/camview.log
Rotating diagnostic log. RTSP credentials are redacted.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B HOME
Used to locate configuration, recordings, snapshots and logs. CamView does not
hard-code a user name.
.TP
.B DISPLAY
X11 display used for the OpenGL context. Native Wayland is not enabled in this
release.
.SH SECURITY
CamView listens only on localhost for RTSPS tunnels and does not open a web
server or a remote-control port. TLS certificate verification in the local
tunnel is disabled for compatibility with self-signed consumer cameras; use
CamView only on a trusted LAN. See
.I /usr/share/doc/camview/SECURITY.md
for the full threat model.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mpv (1),
.BR socat (1),
.BR ffprobe (1)
.PP
Project home page:
.UR https://github.com/orozcorgint/camview
.UE
